**Quick answer:** Greenhouse, Lever, and Workable are generally faster, lighter application experiences, often without a required account. Workday is typically heavier, usually asking you to create an account and re-enter your work history. Large enterprises lean toward Workday, while startups and growth companies commonly use Greenhouse, Lever, and Workable. As a candidate, you do not choose the system, but knowing how each one works helps you apply efficiently.

Most articles that compare applicant tracking systems (ATS) are written for recruiters and HR teams. This one is written for people applying to jobs. We will look at what each platform feels like on your side of the screen, what companies tend to use it, and how to adapt your approach.

One important note: employers configure their ATS differently. Two companies using the same tool can offer slightly different forms and questions. Treat the descriptions below as typical patterns, not guarantees.

